@startuml
title List network flows - filters and pagination
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox

actor Client
boundary "List flows controller" as API
control "Authentication dependency" as Auth
control ListFlowsHandler as Handler
database TimescaleDB as DB

Client -> API : GET /api/v1/flows\nBearer token, optional filters and pagination
API -> Auth : Verify access token
opt Valid access token
    Auth -> DB : SELECT current user's role
    DB --> Auth : user / admin, or no user
end
alt Missing / invalid token or deleted user
    Auth --> API : AuthenticationFailed
    API --> Client : 401 + WWW-Authenticate: Bearer
else Authenticated user / admin
    Auth --> API : Access granted
    API -> API : Validate query parameters
    alt Invalid filters, range or pagination
        API --> Client : 422 {detail: validation errors}
    else Valid query
        API -> Handler : handle(ListFlowsQuery)
        Handler -> DB : One SELECT: filtered flows + page + total\nORDER BY ts_start, flow_id; LIMIT / OFFSET
        DB --> Handler : Page rows and total\ncount retained even for an empty page
        Handler --> API : ListFlowsResponse
        API --> Client : 200 {items, total, page, page_size}
    end
end
note over Auth,DB : A database failure returns 503 through the shared exception handler.
note over Handler,DB : Time range applies to ts_start: [start_time, end_time).\nItems and total share one snapshot; no rows are modified.
@enduml
